ests":["Q6","Q3","Q5"],"summary":"The absence rise is mostly a recording artifact. ShiftLine went live on 2026-03-30 and began logging partial-day absences, which the old process did not record. Full-day absences rose only 1.1%. The independent dispatch log shows unchanged unstaffed trips and late pull-outs, so real attendance did not change. Route groups with no recovery cut and no construction held on-time performance at about 82%. Both groups with cut recovery time fell, and the five construction corridor routes fell most (83.5% to 52.5%). The cause is the April recovery cuts plus the construction lane reductions. Higher early-leave rates on cut routes are confounded by seniority and route length. Do not adopt the discipline program. Restore recovery time, set construction running times, and restate the absence data."},"requestMap":{"X1":"Q5","X2":"Q6","X3":"Q3","X4":"Q4","X5":"Q1","X6":"Q2"}}